## Fox, goose and beans (goose-fox-beans), generated from the Rosie teaching script (english-input.txt) under the world conventions.
##
## Instructor statements used (numbers as in english-input.txt):
##   4. The name of an action is ferry-one.
##   5. You can move the boat and a block on the current bank onto the opposite bank.
##   6. If an object is below a boat then it is current.
##   7. If a location is not below a boat then it is opposite.
##   8. You can move a boat onto the opposite bank.
##  10. If a red block is on an opposite bank and a yellow block is on the opposite bank then you lose.
##  13. If a green block is on an opposite bank and a yellow block is on the opposite bank then you lose.
##  18. The goal is that all the blocks are on a destination bank.
## World: init-fox.world (bank-1; bank-2 named destination; red, yellow and green blocks and the boat, all on bank-1).
##
## Translation (rosie-language.md gives the general reading; the assumption ledger is in README.md):
##   - Operators ferry-one (statement 5; argument1 = the block, argument2 = the opposite bank) and cross (statement 8, not
##     named in the dialog; argument1 = the boat, argument2 = the opposite bank). Moving an object onto a bank replaces its
##     on and below relations; the block and the boat both move in ferry-one.
##   - current (statement 6) is expanded in place: a bank is current when it is below the boat.
##   - opposite (statement 7) tests absence and decides legality, so it is a maintained one-argument relation: each crossing
##     moves opposite from the destination bank to the bank the boat left.
##   - The two losing conditions (statements 10, 13) mark the state with ^failure; look-ahead returns it as a failure.
##   - The goal (statement 18) is ^goal-met true on the task object when no block is on a bank other than the destination
##     bank (A-F3: the boat is a block).

## Propose initialize-goose-fox-beans when its conditions below hold.
sp {goose-fox-beans*propose*initialize-goose-fox-beans
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^world <w> -^name)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <o> + >)
   (<o> ^name initialize-goose-fox-beans ^task-operator false)
}

sp {goose-fox-beans*apply*initialize-goose-fox-beans
   (state <s> ^operator.name initialize-goose-fox-beans ^world <w>)
   (<w> ^objects <objs>)
-->
   (<s> ^name goose-fox-beans ^desireds <ds>)
   (<objs> ^object <o-bank-1> <o-bank-2> <o-red-3> <o-yellow-4> <o-green-5> <o-boat-6> <o-task>)
   (<o-bank-1> ^object-handle bank-1 ^anchored true ^type location ^shape bank)
   (<o-bank-2> ^object-handle bank-2 ^anchored true ^type location ^shape bank ^name destination)
   (<o-red-3> ^object-handle red-3 ^anchored true ^type block ^color red)
   (<o-yellow-4> ^object-handle yellow-4 ^anchored true ^type block ^color yellow)
   (<o-green-5> ^object-handle green-5 ^anchored true ^type block ^color green)
   (<o-boat-6> ^object-handle boat-6 ^anchored true ^type block ^shape boat)
   (<o-task> ^object-handle task ^anchored true ^type task)
   (<ds> ^desired-count 1 ^desired <d1>)
   (<d1> ^object <d1-o>)
   (<d1-o> ^object-handle task ^goal-met true)
   (<w> ^on <on-0>)
   (<on-0> ^argument1 <o-yellow-4> ^argument2 <o-bank-1>)
   (<w> ^on <on-1>)
   (<on-1> ^argument1 <o-green-5> ^argument2 <o-bank-1>)
   (<w> ^on <on-2>)
   (<on-2> ^argument1 <o-boat-6> ^argument2 <o-bank-1>)
   (<w> ^on <on-3>)
   (<on-3> ^argument1 <o-red-3> ^argument2 <o-bank-1>)
   (<w> ^below <below-0>)
   (<below-0> ^argument1 <o-bank-1> ^argument2 <o-yellow-4>)
   (<w> ^below <below-1>)
   (<below-1> ^argument1 <o-bank-1> ^argument2 <o-green-5>)
   (<w> ^below <below-2>)
   (<below-2> ^argument1 <o-bank-1> ^argument2 <o-boat-6>)
   (<w> ^below <below-3>)
   (<below-3> ^argument1 <o-bank-1> ^argument2 <o-red-3>)
   (<w> ^opposite <opposite-bank-2>)
   (<opposite-bank-2> ^argument1 <o-bank-2>)
   (log 1 (crlf) |Initialize goose-fox-beans.|)
}

## Elaborate problem space: adds ^copy-relation, ^dont-copy-object-attribute, ^problem-space.
sp {goose-fox-beans*elaborate*problem-space
   (state <s> ^name goose-fox-beans)
-->
   (<s> ^problem-space <p>)
   (<p> ^name goose-fox-beans ^copy-relation below ^copy-relation opposite ^dont-copy-object-attribute goal-met)
}

sp {goose-fox-beans*elaborate*problem-space*mea-substate
   (state <s> ^impasse no-change ^attribute operator ^superstate <ss>)
   (<ss> ^problem-space.name goose-fox-beans ^operator <so>)
   (<so> ^task-operator true -^pre-conditions-satisfied true)
-->
   (<s> ^problem-space <p>)
   (<p> ^name goose-fox-beans ^dont-copy-object-attribute goal-met)
}

## Elaborate flags: adds ^flag-override, ^mea-operator-selection.
sp {goose-fox-beans*elaborate*flags
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^name goose-fox-beans)
-->
   (<s> ^flag-override <f>)
   (<f> ^mea-operator-selection true)
}

